Package: gnome-shell-extension-incus-monitor
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 46)
Recommends: incus
Description: GNOME Shell extension to monitor and control Incus instances
 Shows the local Incus containers and virtual machines in the top bar with
 their state and resource usage, and lets the user start, stop, restart,
 freeze or open a shell in an instance.
 .
 The extension talks only to the local Incus unix socket and writes to the
 clipboard only when the user chooses "Copy address".
